===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|de|en|to [[handle]]}}. Doublet of etymology 1.

====Alternative form====
* {{l|de|händeln}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈhɛnd(ə)ln/|lang=de}}

====Verb====
{{de-verb-weak|handelt|handelte|gehandelt}}

# {{lb|de|transitive|informal}} to [[handle]] something; to [[control]]; to [[deal]] with in an [[organise]]d fashion
#: {{syn|de|handhaben|bewältigen}}
#: {{ux|de|Wir müssen sehen, wie wir dieses Problem '''handeln'''.|We must find a way of '''handling''' this problem.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Rare in writing for confusability with etymology 1, but fairly common in speech, chiefly in business and media slang.
* The form {{m|de|händeln}} is sometimes used when quoting speech in writing.

